684
00:25:56,870 --> 00:25:59,230
And then we add a -1 to it.

685
00:25:59,230 --> 00:25:59,730
This way,

686
00:25:59,730 --> 00:26:01,370
we get this result.

687
00:26:01,370 --> 00:26:02,430
Think about it, doesn't that make sense?

688
00:26:02,430 --> 00:26:04,650
So for us, actually,

689
00:26:04,650 --> 00:26:06,510
in this kind of special case,

690
00:26:06,510 --> 00:26:07,370
when we construct it,

691
00:26:07,370 --> 00:26:08,250
we need to handle this,

692
00:26:08,250 --> 00:26:10,350
and we have to use this approach to construct it.

693
00:26:10,350 --> 00:26:14,310
That way, we can get this result.

694
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:17,790
The key reason is that for this number after addadd,

695
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:20,070
we have to do sign extension on it.

696
00:26:20,070 --> 00:26:22,430
So this is equivalent to...

697
00:26:22,430 --> 00:26:25,210
As you know, this result is effectively the same as sub,

698
00:26:25,210 --> 00:26:26,350
the effect of subadd,

699
00:26:26,350 --> 00:26:26,590
isn't it?

700
00:26:26,590 --> 00:26:28,310
It's subtracting a 3-bit number.

701
00:26:28,310 --> 00:26:29,790
the concept of subtracting one

702
00:26:29,790 --> 00:26:33,970
Now, some of you might have a question here

703
00:26:33,970 --> 00:26:35,270
